  "title": "Ming dynasty",
  "summary": "The Ming dynasty ruled China from 1368 to 1644, replacing the Mongol Yuan dynasty and restoring a Han ruling house. Its founder, the Hongwu emperor, laid the basis of an authoritarian political culture. With capitals at Nanjing and Beijing, the Ming built the Forbidden City, repaired the Great Wall, sent Zheng He on far-flung voyages and made blue-and-white porcelain. Rebellion and Manchu invasion ended the dynasty in 1644.",
